Use MAX_STATIC_DATA of 500000.
When play begins, seed the random-number generator with 1234.

container is a kind of thing.
door is a kind of thing.
object-like is a kind of thing.
supporter is a kind of thing.
food is a kind of object-like.
key is a kind of object-like.
containers are openable, lockable and fixed in place. containers are usually closed.
door is openable and lockable.
object-like is portable.
supporters are fixed in place.
food is edible.
A room has a text called internal name.


The r_0 and the r_1 and the r_3 and the r_2 and the r_4 and the r_7 and the r_5 and the r_6 are rooms.

Understand "Great Hall" as r_0.
The internal name of r_0 is "Great Hall".
The printed name of r_0 is "-= Great Hall =-".
The Great Hall part 0 is some text that varies. The Great Hall part 0 is "A vaulted hall watched by dusty portraits. A ceremonial plinth stands beneath a cracked glass dome.".
The description of r_0 is "[Great Hall part 0]".

The r_1 is mapped west of r_0.
north of r_0 and south of r_2 is a door called d_0.
east of r_0 and west of r_4 is a door called d_1.
Understand "Library" as r_1.
The internal name of r_1 is "Library".
The printed name of r_1 is "-= Library =-".
The Library part 0 is some text that varies. The Library part 0 is "Tall shelves lean beneath the weight of forgotten books. A writing desk sits in an alcove under the western window.".
The description of r_1 is "[Library part 0]".

The r_0 is mapped east of r_1.
Understand "Astronomer's Study" as r_3.
The internal name of r_3 is "Astronomer's Study".
The printed name of r_3 is "-= Astronomer'S Study =-".
The Astronomer's Study part 0 is some text that varies. The Astronomer's Study part 0 is "Star charts cover the walls. A glass cabinet glitters beside a brass telescope aimed at the ceiling.".
The description of r_3 is "[Astronomer's Study part 0]".

The r_2 is mapped west of r_3.
Understand "launderette" as r_2.
The internal name of r_2 is "launderette".
The printed name of r_2 is "-= Launderette =-".
The launderette part 0 is some text that varies. The launderette part 0 is "Generations of stern manor residents stare from tarnished frames. A narrow passage continues toward the east wing.".
The description of r_2 is "[launderette part 0]".

south of r_2 and north of r_0 is a door called d_0.
The r_6 is mapped north of r_2.
The r_3 is mapped east of r_2.
Understand "Clockwork Workshop" as r_4.
The internal name of r_4 is "Clockwork Workshop".
The printed name of r_4 is "-= Clockwork Workshop =-".
The Clockwork Workshop part 0 is some text that varies. The Clockwork Workshop part 0 is "Silent gears and unfinished mechanisms crowd every surface. A heavy workbench dominates the room.".
The description of r_4 is "[Clockwork Workshop part 0]".

west of r_4 and east of r_0 is a door called d_1.
The r_5 is mapped south of r_4.
Understand "Hidden Vault" as r_7.
The internal name of r_7 is "Hidden Vault".
The printed name of r_7 is "-= Hidden Vault =-".
The Hidden Vault part 0 is some text that varies. The Hidden Vault part 0 is "The air is cold and perfectly still. A carved stone coffer occupies the center of the chamber.".
The description of r_7 is "[Hidden Vault part 0]".

west of r_7 and east of r_5 is a door called d_2.
Understand "Wine Cellar" as r_5.
The internal name of r_5 is "Wine Cellar".
The printed name of r_5 is "-= Wine Cellar =-".
The Wine Cellar part 0 is some text that varies. The Wine Cellar part 0 is "Empty bottle racks line the damp stone walls. A strongbox rests between two collapsed barrels.".
The description of r_5 is "[Wine Cellar part 0]".

The r_4 is mapped north of r_5.
east of r_5 and west of r_7 is a door called d_2.
Understand "Overgrown Courtyard" as r_6.
The internal name of r_6 is "Overgrown Courtyard".
The printed name of r_6 is "-= Overgrown Courtyard =-".
The Overgrown Courtyard part 0 is some text that varies. The Overgrown Courtyard part 0 is "Moonlit ivy has swallowed the old fountain. The manor's tall windows look down on the weeds.".
The description of r_6 is "[Overgrown Courtyard part 0]".

The r_2 is mapped south of r_6.

The c_0 and the c_1 and the c_2 and the c_3 and the c_4 are containers.
The c_0 and the c_1 and the c_2 and the c_3 and the c_4 are privately-named.
The d_0 and the d_1 and the d_2 are doors.
The d_0 and the d_1 and the d_2 are privately-named.
The k_0 and the k_1 and the k_3 and the k_2 are keys.
The k_0 and the k_1 and the k_3 and the k_2 are privately-named.
The o_3 and the o_0 and the o_1 and the o_2 and the o_4 and the o_5 are object-likes.
The o_3 and the o_0 and the o_1 and the o_2 and the o_4 and the o_5 are privately-named.
The r_0 and the r_1 and the r_3 and the r_2 and the r_4 and the r_7 and the r_5 and the r_6 are rooms.
The r_0 and the r_1 and the r_3 and the r_2 and the r_4 and the r_7 and the r_5 and the r_6 are privately-named.
The s_0 and the s_1 and the s_2 and the s_3 and the s_4 are supporters.
The s_0 and the s_1 and the s_2 and the s_3 and the s_4 are privately-named.

